Skia: arm64 SIMD shortcuts also require NEON

A few arm64 shortcuts in Skia and skcms test only for the architecture
(__aarch64__ / SK_CPU_ARM64) and then use NEON types and instructions. With
NEON on, which every normal arm64 build has, the extra condition is always
true and the code is unchanged. It lets the experimental RA64_PIXELS modes
build Skia with NEON off, where these places fall through to the same
portable or SSE code that x86_64 runs.

--- a/include/private/SkHalf.h	2026-10-21 10:46:03.757073491 +0000
+++ b/include/private/SkHalf.h	2026-10-21 10:46:03.874775607 +0000
@@ -40,7 +40,7 @@
 
 static inline Sk4f SkHalfToFloat_finite_ftz(uint64_t rgba) {
     Sk4h hs = Sk4h::Load(&rgba);
-#if !defined(SKNX_NO_SIMD) && defined(SK_CPU_ARM64)
+#if !defined(SKNX_NO_SIMD) && defined(SK_CPU_ARM64) && defined(SK_ARM_HAS_NEON)
     float32x4_t fs;
     asm ("fcvtl %[fs].4s, %[hs].4h   \n"   // vcvt_f32_f16(...)
         : [fs] "=w" (fs)                   // =w: write-only NEON register
@@ -62,7 +62,7 @@
 }
 
